  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 29. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 学区 — 通う学校を決める地域の区分。\n2. 合作 — 複数の人でいっしょに作品を作ること。\n3. 合宿 — いっしょに泊まりながら練習や学習をすること。\n4. 合唱 — 多くの人が声を合わせて歌うこと。\n5. 合奏 — 複数の人が楽器を合わせて演奏すること。\n6. ガッツポーズ — 成功した喜びなどをこぶしや腕の動きで表すこと。\n7. ガラス戸 — ガラスをはめ込んだ戸。\n8. ガレージ — 車を入れておく建物や場所。\n9. 画廊 — 絵などを展示して売る場所。\n10. 眼科 — 目の病気や見え方などを調べて治療する診療科。\n11. 岩礁 — 海面付近などにある岩のまとまり。\n12. 元祖 — ある物事を最初に始めた人や店など。\n13. 頑張り — 目標に向かって力を出して取り組むこと。\n14. 岸壁 — 船を着けるために整えた岸の壁。\n15. 願望 — そうなってほしいと願う気持ち。\n16. ガード — 危険や攻撃などから守ること。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
